; Regression (2026-09-20): a field declared TWICE in one concept. The second
; slot is real layout nobody can reach — every read resolves to the first — and
; nothing looks wrong anywhere: the two declarations may be four hundred lines
; apart and both readers agree, because they read the same slot. It cost
; packages/tscaly a shared memo, and its own Transformer carried a literal
; duplicate line until this gate found it.
; xfail: error: field v of Box is declared twice

define Box (v: int  w: int  v: int)

let b Box(1, 2, 3)
let read b.v
